# W44-AUDIT-5 Phase 2 — Mode C bisect — HONEST-STOP on default-flip
## 2026-05-24

## TL;DR

Mode C (NEW: libjxl Newton math + LS warm-start + LS fallback) produces
**byte-identical output to Mode A** (pre-Phase-2 Zenjxl LS-only refinement)
on every cell of the 3-cell bisect (codec_wiki e7 d=4 + 1418519 + 1531677).
The Mode C default-flip on Zenjxl/Aggressive/LeanFaster was REVERTED
because Mode C is an algorithmic no-op on these inputs — both Newton
paths converge to the same i8 CfL multipliers when starting from
`ls_x` warm-start.

Mode C SHIPS as opt-in API surface only. The W44-AUDIT-5 Phase 1
codec_wiki SSIM2 deficit (-5.51 vs cjxl on `EncoderStrategy::Libjxl`)
remains OPEN — Mode C cannot close it without breaking the Libjxl
byte-lock invariant. Phase 3 would need an orthogonal mechanism (e.g.
lift the screenshot-class discriminator before CfL Pass-1).

## Run command

For each MODE in {A, B, C}:
```bash
JXL_W44_AUDIT_5_FORCE_LS_WARM_START=0 MODE=A \
  ./target/release/examples/w44_audit_5_phase2_mode_bisect
MODE=B ./target/release/examples/w44_audit_5_phase2_mode_bisect
MODE=C ./target/release/examples/w44_audit_5_phase2_mode_bisect
```

Each mode runs codec_wiki + 1418519 + 1531677 at e=7 d=4.0, single-thread,
encode + decode (via jxl-oxide) + SSIM2 (fast_ssim2) + butteraugli
(linear-RGB f32) + cjxl reference.

## Definitions

- **Mode A** (pre-Phase-2 Zenjxl baseline): LS warm-start + LS-only
  refinement using user `eps=1.0 / max_iters=10` from `EffortProfile`
  defaults (the W44-183-shipped path that the W44-29..W44-172
  downstream cost model is calibrated against). Invoked via
  `EncoderStrategy::Zenjxl` + `JXL_W44_AUDIT_5_FORCE_LS_WARM_START=0`
  (forces the new Mode C field OFF).
- **Mode B** (`EncoderStrategy::Libjxl`): bit-exact libjxl CfL Newton
  (eps=100, max_iters=20, start `x=0`, no LS fallback — uses last `x`
  even on non-convergence). Mirrors libjxl `enc_chroma_from_luma.cc:152-167`
  exactly. Required for cjxl byte-parity.
- **Mode C** (NEW Phase 2 hybrid): libjxl Newton math (eps=100,
  max_iters=20) BUT starting from `ls_x` warm-start with LS fallback
  on non-convergence. Encoded as a NEW
  `cfl_newton_libjxl_math_with_ls_warm_start: bool` SIMD parameter +
  matching `EffortProfile` field + matching `EncoderImprovementsCustom`
  gate. `cfl_newton_libjxl_parity = true` (Mode B) takes priority
  inside the SIMD kernel — Mode C only fires when `libjxl_parity =
  false AND libjxl_math_with_ls_warm_start = true`.

